Z||000004||FieroBUZZ||09-12-2001||04:54 PM||||You might try the 'yellow pages' under auto body supplies.  There are probably lots of spots in TO.  Keep in mind you are best off to try to have your primer and finish paint from the same 'line' (Dupont, etc) in order to minimize compatibility probs.<P>P.S. The brush is not a great idea, although I used a roller on a Rambler once!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Gary||||reg||6
Z||000005||Jay||09-12-2001||10:26 PM||||There is a place called Paint City in Scarborough that specializes in automotive paint.  It is at Victoria Park and Mc Nicol Ave.  Don't know what they would charge, depends on how much you buy I guess.<P>------------------<BR>Jay<BR>1986 Northstar GT<BR>www.members.home.net/jaygrande<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cayuga3_3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
